r":null,"queued_ms":1121277,"start_ms":1121277,"first_token_ms":1122497,"end_ms":1136755,"wait_ms":0,"provider_id":"openrouter","model":"stealth/ox-alpha","profile":"STANDARD","effort":"xhigh","input_tokens":4550,"output_tokens":487,"cache_read_tokens":0,"cost_usd":0.0,"thinking_chars":689,"text_chars":1295,"stream_events":166,"stop_reason":"end_turn","outcome":"ok","billed_exact":true,"attempt":1,"fallback_from":null,"retry_reason":null,"has_stream":true},{"id":"hero","agent_id":"hero","phase_id":"phase-4-7","caller":"hero_generator.compose","task":"Paint the day's scene","role":"image","worker":null,"queued_ms":1136756,"start_ms":1136756,"first_token_ms":null,"end_ms":1167738,"wait_ms":0,"provider_id":"image","model":"google/gemini-3-pro-image","profile":"STANDARD","effort":"high","input_tokens":1706,"output_tokens":1120,"image_tokens":1120,"cache_read_tokens":0,"cost_usd":0.137812,"usage_measured":true,"thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":5391,"stream_events":0,"stop_reason":"end_turn","outcome":"ok","attempt":1,"fallback_from":null,"retry_reason":null,"has_stream":false,"image_url":"/data/2026-08-22/hero.webp?v=1787430152","image_prompt":"You are generating a daily hero image for an AI news aggregator website.\n\n## Your Goal\nCreate a playful, colorful editorial illustration that visually represents today's top AI news stories. The scene should immediately convey the themes of the day's news to readers.\n\n## The Mascot (CRITICAL)\nThe attached image shows our skunk mascot. You MUST:\n- Keep the EXACT circuit board pattern on the skunk's body and tail - this is a core part of the brand identity\n- Maintain the skunk's white and black coloring with the tech circuit pattern visible\n- The skunk must be ACTIVELY DOING SOMETHING related to the topics - typing on a keyboard, reading papers, adjusting equipment, pointing at a screen, holding tools, etc. NOT just standing and smiling at the camera!\n- Position the skunk in the lower-left or lower-right portion, engaged with the scene\n\n## Today's Stories\n\n**Topic 1: NVIDIA AVO's Perfect ARC-AGI-3 Score**\nNVIDIA reported that its general-purpose coding agent AVO scored 100% on ARC-AGI-3, completing all 183 levels across 25 public interactive environments. Benchmark creator François Chollet provided authoritative context on Twitter, praising the deep learning-guided on-the-fly synthesis of symbolic world models while cautioning about generalization limits. Reddit communities at r/singularity drove massive engagement but stressed the result was public-set only, and TechCrunch tied the finding to NVIDIA research showing agent harnesses matter more than underlying models.\n**Topic 2: Benchmark Skepticism and Evaluation Methodology**\nA wave of methodological scrutiny cut across every category today. LessWrong posts exposed circularity in standard validation practices, showing shift-by-k-months function vectors on Llama-3.2-3B ace every check yet execute the wrong task, while CHIVE introduced counterfactual prompt experiments to explain unexpected LLM behaviors in the wild. On social media, François Chollet cautioned against overreading ARC-AGI-3 results and Artificial Analysis launched two credibility-focused evaluations, the MLCR-AA medical long-context leaderboard and a Speech Agent Arena. Redditors echoed the distrust, \n**Topic 3: DeepSeek V4-Flash-Vision-Exp Launch**\nDeepSeek released V4-Flash-Vision-Exp, an experimental multimodal model adding image understanding to V4-Flash's text capabilities, claiming parity with Claude Opus 4.8 on agent benchmarks. The Decoder covered the announcement while r/LocalLLaMA hosted same-day launch discussion highlighting DeepSWE results and open-model momentum. The release marks DeepSeek's continued push into vision-capable frontier competition.\n**Topic 4: NVIDIA Compute Empire Expansion**\nNVIDIA dominated infrastructure news with an approximately $12 billion reverse-acquihire of coding startup Poolside, licensing its Model Factory technology while scaling toward 7GW of neocloud capacity, alongside a new partnership with data center developer Cloverleaf. The company also confirmed Vera Rubin is ramping into full production with Microsoft teams, while Starcloud raised $250 million for orbital data centers and Wired profiled Inner Mongolia's emergence as China's critical data center hub. Countervailing signals appeared as well, with a proposed London data center site facing a 1 mi\n**Topic 5: AI Economics: Capex Anxiety Meets Price Cuts**\nEconomic sustainability debates intensified across platforms. Gary Marcus argued on Twitter that AI would need roughly $10 trillion in annual sales to justify current capital expenditure, even as Simile AI raised a $2 billion Series B betting simulation is the next scaling law and Starcloud secured fresh funding. OpenAI simultaneously cut GPT-5.6 Sol API and credit pricing by over 20% for three months, signaling intensifying frontier price competition, and Ethan Mollick predicted an era of contradictions where polls show widespread dislike of AI even as private usage grows. Reddit sentiment mi\n**Topic 6: Model Behavior and Safety Margins Under Scrutiny**\nBehavioral reliability and safety margins drew fire from multiple directions. TechCrunch testing found Claude Opus 4.6, released back in February 2026, can be jailbroken into generating sexually explicit content, while r/ClaudeAI's largest thread of the cycle described Opus 5 as feeling hostile, sparking workaround-sharing and model-routing debates. On the research side, LessWrong posts showed activation steering bypasses refusal in Llama3.1-8B even with benign vectors like Portugal, and that benign off-policy SFT accidentally induces conditional misalignment in Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct. Separately\n\n## Visual Direction\nCreate a scene that represents these stories. You must include Topic 1 (the top story), then pick 2-3 others that would make the best scene together. Consider:\n- What visual metaphors could represent these themes?\n- How can the skunk mascot interact with or observe these elements?\n- Suggested scene elements: performance charts, comparison graphs, trophy, camera lens, image processing, visual recognition, shield icons, protective barriers, guardrails\n\n## Style Requirements\n- Playful cartoon illustration, tech editorial art style\n- Vibrant colors with Trend Red (#E63946) accents\n- Energetic, forward-looking, tech-optimistic mood\n- No company logos or watermarks - but topic-relevant company logos (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) are encouraged when relevant to the stories"}],"concurrency":{"interval_ms":2000,"samples":[[0,0,0],[2000,14,0],[4000,14,0],[6000,14,0],[8000,14,0],[10000,14,0],[12000,14,0],[14000,14,0],[16000,14,0],[18000,14,0],[20000,14,0],[22000,14,0],[24000,14,0],[26000,14,0],[28000,14,0],[30000,14,0],[32000,14,0],[34000,14,0],[36000,14,0],[38000,14,0],[40000,14,0],[42000,14,0],[44000,14,0],[46000,14,0],[48000,14,0],[50000,14,0],[52000,14,0],[54000,14,0],[56000,14,0],[58000,14,0],[60000,14,0],[62000,14,0],[64000,14,0],[66000,13,0],[68000,13,0],[70000,13,0],[72000,13,0],[74000,13,0],[76000,13,0],[78000,13,0],[80000,13,0],[82000,13,0],[84000,13,0],[86000,13,0],[88000,13,0],[90000,13,0],[92000,13,0],[94000,13,0],[96000,13,0],[98000,13,0],[100000,13,0],[102000,13,0],[104000,13,0],[106000,13,0],[108000,13,0],[110000,13,0],[112000,12,0],[114000,12,0],[116000,12,0],[118000,12,0],[120000,12,0],[122000,12,0],[124000,12,0],[126000,12,0],[128000,12,0],[130000,12,0],[132000,12,0],[134000,12,0],[136000,12,0],[138000,12,0],[140000,12,0],[142000,12,0],[144000,12,0],[146000,12,0],[148000,12,0],[150000,12,0],[152000,12,0],[154000,12,0],[156000,12,0],[158000,12,0],[160000,12,0],[162000,11,0],[164000,11,0],[166000,10,0],[168000,10,0],[170000,10,0],[172000,9,0],[174000,9,0],[176000,9,0],[178000,9,0],[180000,9,0],[182000,9,0],[184000,9,0],[186000,8,0],[188000,8,0],[190000,6,0],[192000,6,0],[194000,7,0],[196000,7,0],[198000,7,0],[200000,7,0],[202000,6,0],[204000,6,0],[